# One CI gate, one file. Issue #991 moved the gate list out of
# `.github/workflows/release.yml`, the repository's third most conflicted path,
# because its step list was append-only. A gate lives here instead, so two
# branches adding gates create two files, never one shared region.
# `rust-script scripts/run-ci-gates.rs --stage <stage>` runs them.
ci_gate check-hardcoded-language-js-twin
  stage rust
  description "scripts/check-hardcoded-language.mjs prints exactly what scripts/check-hardcoded-language.rs prints, with the same exit code, so agents can run the JavaScript twin instead of compiling Rust."
  run "node scripts/lib/checks-twin-parity.mjs check-hardcoded-language"
  justification "Coding agents run the JavaScript twin because compiling Rust scripts locally filled the rust-script cache to 3.7 GB (PR #1188); a twin that drifted from the Rust gate would pass work that CI then rejects."
